<div>
  <p>Hey <%= @seller.name_or_username %>,</p>
  <p>We'll soon unify your refund policies. Instead of each product having its own policy, all your products will now use a single account-level policy.</p>
  <p>
    As part of becoming a <%= link_to "Merchant of Record", "https://gumroad.gumroad.com/p/gumroad-is-becoming-a-merchant-of-record-more-updates", target: "_blank" %>,
    starting January, every product will follow the same refund policy for new purchases.
    <br>
    It also means that—soon—we'll be able to handle refund requests on your behalf, saving you time and energy.
  </p>
  <p>Two refund policy options will be available:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>30-day money back guarantee (default)</li>
    <li>No refunds allowed</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>No action is needed</strong>—we'll notify you in January once your account is migrated.</p>
</div>
<div>
  <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
  <h4>What will be my default refund policy?</h4>
  <p>If all your products have a <em>no refunds</em> policy, we'll use that as your default. Otherwise, we'll use the <em>30-day money back guarantee</em>.</p>
  <h4>Can I set different refund policies for different products?</h4>
  <p>No, all your products will share the same refund policy to simplify the experience for you and your customers.</p>
  <h4>What happens to existing purchases?</h4>
  <p>Purchases made before this change will keep their original refund policy that was in place at the time of purchase.</p>
  <h4>Can I change my refund policy later?</h4>
  <p>Yes, you can switch between the two options anytime after migration. The new policy will apply to all new purchases.</p>
</div>
<div>
  <p>More questions? Just reply to this email.</p>
</div>
